module

public import Mathlib
public import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.EllipticCurve.Affine.Point.Galois
public import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.EllipticCurve.TateModule.Galois
public import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.EllipticCurve.Isogeny.Hom.Ring

/-!
# KatoEulerSystems: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. It states the roadmap's headline
theorems against the pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti APIs. Serre's open-image theorem of §4.7 is
statable on the Tau Ceti Tate-module representation, with non-CM expressed through the Tau Ceti
endomorphism ring of the curve over the algebraic closure. The elliptic cases of §7.9 are statable:
finite generation over every fixed cyclotomic tower, and finiteness of the Mordell–Weil χ-part
over cyclotomic fields when the continued twisted L-function is nonzero at 1, whose case m = 1
is finiteness of rational points at analytic rank zero. They carry no modularity hypothesis:
every elliptic curve over ℚ is modular (EllipticCurveModularity, R29.6).

Beilinson's real regulator formula (§3.4) lacks the K₂ group of the modular curve with its
regulator map and the operator-valued zeta function. The canonical zeta morphisms
(§§5.1, 5.4, 5.6), the module structure of Iwasawa cohomology (§4.4), the finite index of the
smoothed integral span (§5.2), the critical interpolation (§5.3), non-torsion and the
cohomological bound (§§7.1–7.2) lack Iwasawa cohomology and the modular Galois realization.
Perrin-Riou's map for de Rham representations (§6.1) lacks Iwasawa cohomology of local Galois
representations, D_crys and D_dR, and the distribution algebras ℋ_h. The regulator
equality (§6.4) lacks the Kato zeta morphism and analytic p-adic L-function. The
ordinary and multiplicative divisibility (§7.4) lacks the Iwasawa Selmer module over
ℚ_∞ and the Mazur–Swinnerton-Dyer p-adic L-function; absence of finite submodules
(§7.6) lacks that Selmer module. The Bloch–Kato finiteness theorem (§7.9, parts 1–2)
lacks the Selmer groups of V_λ(f), and the Tamagawa bound there lacks its Galois
cohomology and canonical zeta class. The abelian-variety conclusions of §7.9 lack
A_f and J₁(N). The Selmer χ-part (Corollary 14.3(1)) lacks the `p^∞`-Selmer group of E
over K; Tau Ceti's `selmerGroup₂` is the 2-Selmer group, finite without any L-value
hypothesis. Classical finiteness and the rank-zero upper bound for the Tate–Shafarevich
group (§§7.3, 7.8) lack the topological Galois module E(ℚ̄) and its local restriction
maps, although Mathlib has ContinuousCohomology.tateShafarevich for supplied Galois modules.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace TauCetiRoadmap.KatoEulerSystems

/-! ## Layer 4: image, nonvanishing and Iwasawa inputs before the canonical map -/

/-- Serre's open-image theorem for an elliptic curve over ℚ without complex multiplication,
that is, every endomorphism of the curve over the algebraic closure of ℚ is multiplication by
an integer. For every prime ℓ the image of the absolute Galois group in the automorphism group
of the ℓ-adic Tate module has finite index (equivalently it is open, being compact), and it is
the whole automorphism group for all but finitely many ℓ (Serre 1972, Théorèmes 2–3). -/
theorem serre_openImage (W : WeierstrassCurve ℚ) [W.IsElliptic]
    [DecidableEq (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)]
    (hW : ∀ φ : TauCeti.Isogeny.Hom (W.baseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)).toAffine
        (W.baseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)).toAffine, ∃ n : ℤ, φ = n) :
    (∀ (ℓ : ℕ) [Fact ℓ.Prime],
      ((W.tateModuleGaloisRepresentation (K := AlgebraicClosure ℚ) ℓ).asGroupHom.range
        ).FiniteIndex) ∧
    {ℓ : ℕ | ∃ _ : Fact ℓ.Prime,
      (W.tateModuleGaloisRepresentation (K := AlgebraicClosure ℚ) ℓ).asGroupHom.range
        ≠ ⊤}.Finite := by
  sorry

/-! ## Layer 7: divisibility and elliptic applications -/

/-- For an elliptic curve over ℚ and every integer m ≥ 1, its points over ⋃ₙ ℚ(ζ_(mⁿ)) form a
finitely generated abelian group, including CM curves and m = 1. This is the elliptic case of
Kato, Theorem 14.4. The field is the subfield of ℂ generated by all m-power roots of unity. -/
theorem ellipticCyclotomicFiniteGeneration (W : WeierstrassCurve ℚ) [W.IsElliptic]
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 1 ≤ m) :
    AddGroup.FG (W.baseChange (IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ
      {x : ℂ | ∃ n : ℕ, x ^ (m ^ n) = 1})).toAffine.Point := by
  sorry

/-- For an elliptic curve over ℚ, its K-points killed by the kernel of
ℤ[Gal(K/ℚ)] → ℂ induced by ψ. A group-ring element acts by the integral linear
combination of the actual coordinate actions, retaining all torsion. This is Kato's
χ-part (14.2, p. 235) specialized to elliptic points. -/
noncomputable def ellipticCharacterPart (W : WeierstrassCurve ℚ) [W.IsElliptic]
    (K : Type*) [Field K] [DecidableEq K] [Algebra ℚ K]
    (ψ : (K ≃ₐ[ℚ] K) →* ℂ) : Set (W.baseChange K).toAffine.Point :=
  {P | ∀ a : MonoidAlgebra ℤ (K ≃ₐ[ℚ] K),
    MonoidAlgebra.lift ℤ ℂ (K ≃ₐ[ℚ] K) ψ a = 0 →
      a.coeff.sum (fun σ n => n • Multiplicative.toAdd (W.pointGaloisAction σ) P) = 0}

/-- For an elliptic curve over ℚ, the χ-part of its points over any m-th cyclotomic
field is finite if the continued χ-twisted L-function is nonzero at 1 (Kato,
Corollary 14.3(2)). The Galois character sends ζ_m ↦ ζ_m^a to χ(a), and the Dirichlet
series uses the zero extension modulo m, including imprimitive χ. Its value at 1 is taken
from the entire continuation, which agrees with the total Dirichlet sum on Re(s) > 3/2; no
value of that sum at s = 1 is used. For m = 1 the character part is all of E(ℚ) and the
series is the elliptic L-series, so this includes finiteness of E(ℚ) when L(E,1) ≠ 0. -/
theorem ellipticCharacterPoints_finite (W : WeierstrassCurve ℚ) [W.IsElliptic]
    (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] (K : Type*) [Field K] [DecidableEq K] [Algebra ℚ K]
    [IsCyclotomicExtension {m} ℚ K] (χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ m)
    (F : ℂ → ℂ) (hF : Differentiable ℂ F)
    (hcont : ∀ s : ℂ, 3 / 2 < s.re →
      F s = LSeries (fun n => (W.LFunction n : ℂ) * χ n) s)
    (hne : F 1 ≠ 0) :
    (ellipticCharacterPart W K
      ((Units.coeHom ℂ).comp (χ.toUnitHom.comp
        (IsCyclotomicExtension.autEquivPow K
          (Polynomial.cyclotomic.irreducible_rat (NeZero.pos m))).toMonoidHom))).Finite := by
  sorry

end TauCetiRoadmap.KatoEulerSystems
